# xgs-ntb-watch.sh sources this file if it exists.
#
# 1 = allow ONE automatic `xgs-ntb-up.sh --force-rescan` after the link has been
# unhealthy for LIMIT*INTERVAL (5 min); it then cools down for 10 min.
#
# Measured 2026-11-25, twice: an NPU reboot never brings this end back by
# itself.  eth0 stays at operstate DOWN with "endpoint unreachable, dropping
# doorbell" in dmesg, and because the only route to this machine is the vNTB
# link (PC -> NPU br-lan -> eth0.200 -> here) the box becomes unreachable
# exactly when it is needed -- the serial console is the only way in.  So the
# watcher recovers on its own now.
#
# Why the 5 minute delay: a remove/rescan re-asserts PERST# and would interrupt
# an NPU that is still booting.  The NPU's Linux is up in 11 s, so waiting five
# minutes costs nothing and removes that failure mode.
AUTO_RECOVER=1
MAX_RECOVER=1
